---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is the DNS security section?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "It's a curated collection of guides and tools focused on dns security, organized from fundamentals to advanced configurations."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Are all these pages free?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: every guide and tool on PromptDNS is free forever, with no account and no limits."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I navigate this section?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Start with the first card and follow the internal links. Each page connects to related topics so you naturally build understanding."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How often is this content updated?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Money pages are reviewed and refreshed every 90 days. New guides are added weekly as the topical map expands."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I suggest a topic that's missing?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: email hello@promptdns.com with your suggestion. We prioritize based on search demand and user feedback."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this content written by experts?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Every page follows a documented editorial standard: verified processes, tool-verified instructions, and regular reviews. See the About page for details."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DNS Security: Hijacking, Poisoning, Tunneling & Defense"
  description="DNS security cluster: hijacking, cache poisoning, amplification attacks, tunneling, rebinding — how each attack works and the layered defense that stops them."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DNS Security</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DNS Security</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      DNS is the internet's trust layer: every website visit, email delivery, and API call
      depends on DNS answers being correct. These guides cover the attacks that exploit DNS
      and the defenses that stop them.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink border-b border-line pb-3 mb-4">Attack Types</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        {[
          { href: '/dns-hijacking/', title: 'DNS Hijacking', desc: 'Registrar compromise, on-path interception, cache poisoning. How attacks work and the layered defense.' },
          { href: '/dns-cache-poisoning/', title: 'Cache Poisoning', desc: 'How forged records end up in resolver caches, the Kaminsky attack, and why DNSSEC is the answer.' },
          { href: '/dns-amplification-attack/', title: 'Amplification Attacks', desc: 'How open resolvers are weaponized for DDoS, and how to prevent your server from being used.' },
          { href: '/dns-tunneling/', title: 'DNS Tunneling', desc: 'Data exfiltration through DNS queries, detection signals, and prevention.' },
          { href: '/dns-rebinding-explained/', title: 'DNS Rebinding', desc: 'Bypassing the same-origin policy using DNS time gaps to access internal networks.' },
        ].map((s) => (
          <a href={s.href} class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5 transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-accent/40">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-accent">{s.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-dim">{s.desc}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink border-b border-line pb-3 mb-4">Defense</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        {[
          { href: '/what-is-dnssec/', title: 'DNSSEC', desc: 'Cryptographically signed answers that make forgeries detectable.' },
          { href: '/dnssec-checker/', title: 'DNSSEC Checker', desc: 'Verify your DS records, DNSKEYs, and algorithm strength.' },
          { href: '/caa-record/', title: 'CAA Records', desc: 'Restrict which CAs can issue certificates for your domain.' },
        ].map((s) => (
          <a href={s.href} class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5 transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-accent/40">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-accent">{s.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-dim">{s.desc}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-accent/25 bg-gradient-to-br from-accent/10 to-violet/10 p-6">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
        <strong class="text-ink">Verify your security posture:</strong> run the
        <a href="/" class="font-medium text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">homepage security scanner</a> (DNSSEC,
        SPF, DKIM, DMARC in one pass), then confirm records with the
        <a href="/dns-record-lookup/" class="font-medium text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS record lookup</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the DNS security section?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">It's a curated collection of guides and tools focused on dns security, organized from fundamentals to advanced configurations.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Are all these pages free?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: every guide and tool on PromptDNS is free forever, with no account and no limits.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I navigate this section?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Start with the first card and follow the internal links. Each page connects to related topics so you naturally build understanding.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How often is this content updated?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Money pages are reviewed and refreshed every 90 days. New guides are added weekly as the topical map expands.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I suggest a topic that's missing?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: email hello@promptdns.com with your suggestion. We prioritize based on search demand and user feedback.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this content written by experts?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Every page follows a documented editorial standard: verified processes, tool-verified instructions, and regular reviews. See the About page for details.</p></details></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
